  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the centres of the circles <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> respectively. If <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> are the points of intersection of these circles, then the area (in sq. units) of the quadrilateral <math><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KQE6X",
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RMStm",
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JHgal",
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SaH4w",
      "text": "<math><mn>9</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of given circles are</p><p><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/wpavgyhjbvuhkwscirkzzgpdcxmlwgdsawotvbhwhzogmhjcdy.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 208px;\" /></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>; <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now, by distance formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#8736;</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(by converse of pythagoras&nbsp;theorem in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>)</p><p>Hence, area of quadrilateral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo></math>area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo></math>area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>",
